import{_ as e,c as o,o as i,a3 as t}from"./chunks/framework.Bsyxd66g.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Notifications","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"subsystems/notifications.md","filePath":"subsystems/notifications.md","lastUpdated":1794137243000}'),d={name:"subsystems/notifications.md"},a=t('<h1 id="notifications" tabindex="-1">Notifications <a class="header-anchor" href="#notifications" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Notifications&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="responsibility-and-boundaries" tabindex="-1">Responsibility and boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#responsibility-and-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Responsibility and boundaries&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Owns: the <code>Notifier</code> configuration variants (Telegram, Webhook, SMTP), message rendering (Telegram text/photo, webhook handlebars payloads and headers, SMTP MIME structure), the <code>Message</code> payload, the &quot;new videos downloaded&quot; digest (<code>DownloadNotifyInfo</code>), the decision to send or suppress, and the test-send endpoint behavior.</li><li>Does not own: the config storage format (<a href="./config-and-persistence">config-and-persistence.md</a>); when errors occur (<a href="./sync-pipeline">sync-pipeline.md</a>, <a href="./bilibili-client">bilibili-client.md</a>); the settings UI (<a href="./web-ui">web-ui.md</a>); the HTTP route plumbing beyond its payload (<a href="./web-api-server">web-api-server.md</a>).</li><li>Talks to: <code>Config::notifiers</code>, <code>TEMPLATE</code> (webhook templates), the shared <code>reqwest::Client</code> from <code>BiliClient::inner_client()</code>, and the call sites <code>notify</code> / <code>error_and_notify</code> in <code>utils/notify.rs</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="sources-of-truth" tabindex="-1">Sources of truth <a class="header-anchor" href="#sources-of-truth" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Sources of truth&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Authoritative types and transports: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/notifier/mod.rs</code> (<code>Notifier</code>, <code>SmtpEncryption</code>, <code>webhook_template_key</code>, <code>webhook_template_content</code>, <code>Notifier::notify</code>, <code>notifier::NotifierAllExt::notify_all</code>).</li><li>Authoritative payload/format: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/notifier/message.rs</code> (<code>Message</code>, conversions) and <code>crates/bili_sync/src/notifier/info.rs</code> (<code>DownloadNotifyInfo::{new,record,should_notify}</code>).</li><li>Authoritative send policy: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/utils/notify.rs</code> (<code>notify</code>, <code>error_and_notify</code>).</li><li>Authoritative webhook template registration: <code>crates/bili_sync/src/config/handlebar.rs</code> (<code>create_template</code> registers every webhook under <code>payload_{url}</code>).</li><li>Forbidden duplicate sources: hard-coded webhook bodies in call sites, a second HTTP client for notifications, or per-run copies of the notifier list (it is snapshotted from the config).</li></ul><h2 id="main-paths-change-loci" tabindex="-1">Main paths / change loci <a class="header-anchor" href="#main-paths-change-loci" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Main paths / change loci&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Key entry points: <ul><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/notifier/mod.rs</code> (<code>Notifier::notify</code>, <code>notify_all</code>).</li><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/utils/notify.rs</code> (<code>notify</code>, <code>error_and_notify</code>).</li><li><code>crates/bili_sync/src/api/routes/config/mod.rs</code> (<code>ping_notifiers</code>, route <code>POST /api/config/notifiers/ping</code>).</li></ul></li><li>Common edit locations: <ul><li>New channel: add a <code>Notifier</code> variant, a <code>notify_internal</code> arm, the settings form in <code>web/src/routes/settings/NotifierDialog.svelte</code>, and the <code>Notifier</code> type in <code>web/src/lib/types.ts</code>.</li><li>New digest wording: <code>Message</code> conversions in <code>message.rs</code> and the switch threshold in <code>DownloadNotifyInfo::record</code>.</li><li>Webhook default body/template: <code>webhook_template_content</code> and <code>create_template</code>.</li><li>Suppression rules: <code>error_and_notify</code> and <code>BiliError::is_common_error</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Call sites: <ul><li><code>workflow::process_video_source</code> sends one digest per source after downloading (<code>notify</code> when <code>should_notify()</code>).</li><li><code>task::video_downloader</code> sends failures for: scheduler init (<code>初始化视频下载任务失败…</code>), job reload (<code>重载视频下载任务失败…</code>), credential check (<code>本轮凭据检查与刷新任务执行遇到错误…</code>), a failed round (<code>本轮视频下载任务执行遇到错误…</code>), and a per-source failure (<code>处理 {} 时遇到错误：{:#}，跳过该视频源</code>).</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="runtime-paths-and-state-transitions" tabindex="-1">Runtime paths and state transitions <a class="header-anchor" href="#runtime-paths-and-state-transitions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Runtime paths and state transitions&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Trigger / inputs / outputs / interfaces: <ul><li>Inputs: <code>Config::notifiers: Option&lt;Arc&lt;Vec&lt;Notifier&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> and a <code>Message { message, image_url }</code>.</li><li>Outputs: side effects only — HTTP requests to Telegram/webhook endpoints or an SMTP conversation. <code>notify</code> returns <code>()</code>; <code>notify_all</code> returns <code>Result&lt;()&gt;</code> that is always <code>Ok</code>.</li><li>Templates: webhook bodies are handlebars templates registered under <code>payload_{url}</code> from <code>Config.notifiers</code> whenever the config changes.</li></ul></li><li>Main execution path (source files and named symbols): <ol><li><code>notify(config, bili_client, msg)</code> returns immediately when <code>notifiers</code> is <code>None</code> or empty; otherwise it clones the notifier list and the <code>reqwest::Client</code> and spawns <code>notify_all</code> as a detached task (fire-and-forget; the sync pipeline never waits for delivery).</li><li><code>error_and_notify(config, bili_client, msg, error)</code> logs the message at <code>error!</code> first, then returns early when <code>config.ignore_common_errors</code> is true <strong>and</strong> any cause in the error chain is a <code>BiliError</code> recognized by <code>is_common_error</code> (<code>-503 服务暂不可用</code>, <code>-504 服务调用超时</code>). Otherwise it spawns <code>notify_all</code> the same way.</li><li><code>notify_all</code> runs all notifiers with <code>future::join_all</code> and discards each result, so one failing channel never blocks or reports against another. Delivery failures are not surfaced anywhere except inside each transport&#39;s <code>?</code> (which becomes a dropped <code>Result</code>).</li><li>Telegram: with an <code>image_url</code> and <code>skip_image == false</code>, a <code>sendPhoto</code> form (<code>chat_id</code>, <code>photo</code>, <code>caption</code>); otherwise <code>sendMessage</code> (<code>chat_id</code>, <code>text</code>).</li><li>Webhook: renders the payload — cached template <code>payload_{url}</code> normally, or an inline render of <code>webhook_template_content(template)</code> when <code>ignore_cache</code> is set (the test endpoint sets it). The default template is <code>{&quot;text&quot;: &quot;{{{message}}}&quot;}</code>. Always sets <code>Content-Type: application/json</code>, then applies any custom <code>headers</code> that parse as valid <code>HeaderName</code>/<code>HeaderValue</code> (invalid pairs are silently skipped).</li><li>SMTP: builds a lettre message with subject <code>BiliSync 通知</code>. With an <code>image_url</code>, it downloads the image (requires a <code>Content-Type</code>), embeds it as an inline attachment with a random <code>cid</code>, and sends <code>multipart/alternative</code> (plain text + <code>multipart/related</code> HTML with the escaped message and an <code>&lt;img src=&quot;cid:…&quot;&gt;</code>); without an image it sends a plain-text-only message. Transport choice: <code>None</code> → <code>builder_dangerous(host)</code>, <code>Tls</code> → <code>relay(host)</code>, <code>StartTls</code> → <code>starttls_relay(host)</code>, always <code>.port(port)</code>. Credentials are added only when <code>username</code> or <code>password</code> is non-empty.</li><li>The test endpoint <code>POST /api/config/notifiers/ping</code> deserializes a single <code>Notifier</code>, forces <code>ignore_cache</code> for webhooks, and sends <code>This is a test notification from BiliSync.</code> with the project&#39;s socialify image URL, returning the transport error as an <code>ApiError</code> (unlike production sends).</li><li><code>DownloadNotifyInfo</code> accumulates the digest per source: <code>record</code> keeps only models whose five subtask values are all <code>STATUS_OK</code> and that are not in <code>excluded_video_ids</code> (videos that were only re-synced for danmaku). Beyond 10 titles it collapses to a <code>Summary</code> count. <code>should_notify</code> is false only while still in list mode with no titles.</li></ol></li><li>State ownership, transitions and persistence: <ul><li>Notifier configuration lives only in <code>Config</code>; nothing about delivery is persisted (no retry queue, no last-sent marker).</li><li><code>DownloadNotifyInfo::List</code> → <code>Summary</code> is the only internal state transition, triggered by the 10-title threshold; subsequent records only increment the count.</li><li><code>Message</code> is built from either a <code>&amp;str</code>/<code>String</code> (no image) or a <code>DownloadNotifyInfo</code> (optional cover image).</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="constraints-and-failures" tabindex="-1">Constraints and failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#constraints-and-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Constraints and failures&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Invariants: <ul><li>Notifications must never block or fail the sync pipeline: both <code>notify</code> and <code>error_and_notify</code> spawn detached tasks.</li><li>The digest counts only videos whose five subtasks are all <code>STATUS_OK</code>; a video with a failed artifact must not be announced.</li><li>Videos that were re-synced only for danmaku (<code>excluded_video_ids</code>) must not be announced as new.</li><li>Webhook payloads are handlebars templates; escaping depends on the template author (<code>{{{message}}}</code> is unescaped).</li></ul></li><li>Failure modes and recovery: <ul><li>Delivery errors are swallowed by <code>notify_all</code>; users see nothing but the server log line from <code>error_and_notify</code> (if any). There is no retry — the next run produces a new digest for new videos only.</li><li>A malformed webhook template makes <code>create_template</code> fail. If this occurs during <code>TEMPLATE</code> initialization, initialization fails; on a later config update, <code>VersionedCache</code> logs the error and retains the previous template cache. A notification using that stale cache can fail to render, and <code>notify_all</code> discards the delivery error.</li><li>SMTP with a missing image <code>Content-Type</code> fails that send (<code>Missing image Content-Type</code>); a <code>None</code>-encryption server without authentication is supported via <code>builder_dangerous</code>.</li><li><code>ignore_common_errors</code> suppresses only <code>-503</code>/<code>-504</code>; all other errors are notified.</li></ul></li><li>Compatibility / migration behavior: <ul><li><code>Notifier</code> is <code>#[serde(tag = &quot;type&quot;, rename_all = &quot;camelCase&quot;)]</code>, stored inside the config JSON blob. Variant/field renames break existing databases; add <code>#[serde(default)]</code> for new fields.</li><li><code>SmtpEncryption</code> serializes as <code>none</code>/<code>tls</code>/<code>starttls</code> (<code>rename_all = &quot;lowercase&quot;</code>).</li><li>The webhook <code>ignore_cache</code> field is <code>#[serde(skip)]</code> and exists only for the test path; it must not be persisted or sent by clients.</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="forbidden-patterns-and-common-mistakes" tabindex="-1">Forbidden patterns and common mistakes <a class="header-anchor" href="#forbidden-patterns-and-common-mistakes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Forbidden patterns and common mistakes&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Forbidden: awaiting <code>notify_all</code> inline in the pipeline or returning its error to the caller; delivery is best-effort by design.</li><li>Forbidden: sending the <code>auth_token</code>, cookies or the full config through notifiers. Only the explicit <code>Message</code> is sent.</li><li>Forbidden: adding a per-notifier retry loop; there is no durable queue, and a retry would duplicate digests.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting <code>notify_all</code> to report failures. It always returns <code>Ok(())</code>; only <code>Notifier::notify</code> (used by the ping endpoint) propagates errors.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting webhook headers to be validated/saved. Invalid header names/values are skipped at send time without an error.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting the digest to list every downloaded video. Only fully successful ones are counted, and the list collapses to a summary above 10.</li><li>Common mistake: expecting the Telegram image to be a local file. <code>sendPhoto</code> takes the remote <code>image_url</code> the server passes through (for the digest it is the first successful video&#39;s cover).</li><li>Common mistake: expecting SMTP to always send multipart. Without an <code>image_url</code> it is a plain-text single part, and the subject is fixed.</li><li>Common mistake: assuming the test endpoint and production sends share rendering behavior. The test path sets <code>ignore_cache</code>, so it always renders the freshly submitted template, while production uses the template registered in <code>TEMPLATE</code> from the saved config.</li></ul><h2 id="how-to-verify" tabindex="-1">How to verify <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-to-verify" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How to verify&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Manual: add a webhook notifier in the settings UI and click test (<code>POST /api/config/notifiers/ping</code>); confirm the receiver gets the test body and that a wrong URL surfaces an error in the UI (the ping endpoint returns it).</li><li>Manual: enable a Telegram notifier with <code>skip_image</code> toggled and compare <code>sendPhoto</code> vs <code>sendMessage</code>; the digest message starts with <code>&lt;source&gt;的 N 条新视频已入库</code>.</li><li>Manual: configure SMTP with <code>None</code>, <code>Tls</code> and <code>StartTls</code> against a local mail catcher and verify subject <code>BiliSync 通知</code>, inline image presence, and that credentials are only used when filled.</li><li>Manual: sync a source with more than 10 new videos and confirm the message switches from a numbered list to <code>… 条新视频已入库，快去看看吧！</code>.</li><li>Manual: trigger a <code>-503</code> error with <code>ignore_common_errors</code> enabled and confirm only the log line appears and no notification is sent; disable it and confirm the notification arrives.</li><li>Existing checks: <code>cargo test -p bili_sync</code>, <code>cargo clippy -- -D warnings</code>, <code>cargo +nightly fmt --check</code> (there is no dedicated notifier unit test in-tree).</li></ul>',15),n=[a];function s(c,r,l,h,u,f){return i(),o("div",null,n)}const g=e(d,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,g as default};
